export default JSON.parse("{\"1.6.2\":{\"unit\":\"1.6\",\"courseId\":\"1.6.2\",\"hook\":{\"prompt\":\"Which of these plan lines can the app check for you?\",\"control\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"trend\",\"label\":\"Trade with the trend\",\"feedback\":\"Which trend, on which timeframe, measured how? Two people could disagree, so no app can check it.\"},{\"id\":\"risk\",\"label\":\"Risk 1% of current equity per trade\",\"feedback\":\"Right. The ticket shows the stop, the size and your equity, so the risk can be checked before the order goes in.\"},{\"id\":\"patient\",\"label\":\"Be patient\",\"feedback\":\"A good intention, but not a rule. Nothing on a ticket shows whether you were patient.\"}],\"answer\":\"risk\"},\"compare\":\"You picked “{yours}”. Only “Risk 1% of current equity per trade” is a number the app can check on every ticket. The other two are intentions.\",\"concept\":\"trading-plan\"},\"learn\":[{\"kind\":\"explain\",\"title\":\"Start small\",\"text\":\"Your first written [[trading-plan|plan]], v1, is short, checkable and has **one setup**. Short, because you'll actually read it. Checkable, because every rule can be answered yes or no from a chart or a ticket. One setup, because 30 trades of one setup tell you something; 30 trades spread over five setups tell you very little.\"},{\"kind\":\"figure\",\"title\":\"The sections of plan v1\",\"text\":\"Eight sections, each with an example line. Yours will say different things; the shape stays the same.\",\"figure\":{\"kind\":\"flow\",\"start\":\"goal\",\"nodes\":[{\"id\":\"goal\",\"text\":\"Goal and constraints, with your risk capital\",\"kind\":\"end\"},{\"id\":\"market\",\"text\":\"Market and timeframes\",\"kind\":\"end\"},{\"id\":\"setup\",\"text\":\"One setup, with yes-or-no conditions\",\"kind\":\"end\"},{\"id\":\"risk\",\"text\":\"Risk rules: per trade, per day, trades per day\",\"kind\":\"end\"},{\"id\":\"exits\",\"text\":\"Exits: stop, target, time\",\"kind\":\"end\"},{\"id\":\"routine\",\"text\":\"Routine: before, during and after the session\",\"kind\":\"end\"},{\"id\":\"journal\",\"text\":\"Journal and review\",\"kind\":\"end\"},{\"id\":\"changes\",\"text\":\"Rule for changes\",\"kind\":\"end\"}],\"steps\":[\"Goal: learn the process over 30 trades, using only risk capital. Market: LABX, 1H chart.\",\"Setup: pullback in an uptrend, with three conditions, each yes or no.\",\"Risk: 1% per trade, stop for the day at −3R, three trades a day at most.\",\"Exits: stop, 2R target or time. Checklist before, journal after, weekly review. Changes only by the rule.\"]},\"concept\":\"trading-plan\"},{\"kind\":\"worked\",\"title\":\"Risk capital\",\"lines\":[\"Savings, in any currency: 20,000.\",\"Emergency fund, six months of expenses: 12,000.\",\"Already promised, next year's tuition: 5,000.\",\"[[risk-capital|Risk capital]] = 20,000 − 12,000 − 5,000 = ?\"],\"ask\":{\"answer\":3000,\"tolerance\":0,\"feedback\":[{\"value\":8000,\"text\":\"That keeps the tuition in. Money already promised can't be lost either: subtract it too.\"},{\"value\":15000,\"text\":\"That keeps the emergency fund in. It's there for emergencies, not for trading: subtract it.\"}],\"correct\":\"Right: 3,000. Only this money belongs in a trading account. Here it's virtual; the habit isn't.\"},\"after\":\"Risk capital is money you could lose entirely without touching living costs, debts or emergency savings. Your plan's limits sit inside it.\",\"concept\":\"risk-capital\"},{\"kind\":\"match\",\"title\":\"Vague or checkable?\",\"prompt\":\"A plan line is only useful if anyone could check it, on the chart or the ticket, and get the same answer. Match each vague line to its checkable version.\",\"columns\":[\"Vague\",\"Checkable\"],\"pairs\":[{\"left\":\"The trend is up\",\"right\":\"The last two swing highs and lows are each higher than the ones before\",\"wrong\":\"'Up' needs a test anyone can run: compare the last swing highs and lows.\"},{\"left\":\"Don't risk too much\",\"right\":\"Risk 1% of current equity, costs included\",\"wrong\":\"'Too much' is about money on one trade: a percentage of equity, with costs.\"},{\"left\":\"Stop if it's a bad day\",\"right\":\"Stop for the day after −3R\",\"wrong\":\"'A bad day' needs a number: the loss in R after which the session ends.\"},{\"left\":\"Use a sensible stop\",\"right\":\"Stop 0.20 below the pullback low\",\"wrong\":\"'Sensible' needs a place: a fixed distance beyond the level that proves the idea wrong.\"}],\"correct\":\"Each checkable line names a number or a test. If two people could disagree about a line, rewrite it.\",\"concept\":\"trading-plan\"},{\"kind\":\"explain\",\"title\":\"Versions\",\"text\":\"Your plan starts as **v1.0**. Change a rule only after at least 30 trades with it, or when a clear breach shows a gap in the plan; never during a session; always with the reason written. The new version, v1.1, starts a fresh count. Rules changed after every loss never get tested.\"},{\"kind\":\"callout\",\"tone\":\"key\",\"text\":\"Your plan is the yardstick. **Decision Quality** and **Risk Discipline** measure each trade against it, so write its limits as numbers that can be checked on every ticket.\"},{\"kind\":\"order\",\"title\":\"Write plan v1\",\"prompt\":\"Now write yours. Put the steps in order, from what limits you to what you'll do. Then write your one setup in a line.\",\"items\":[\"Work out your risk capital.\",\"Pick one market and the timeframes you read.\",\"Write one setup as yes-or-no conditions.\",\"Set risk per trade, the daily limit and the maximum trades a day.\",\"Add exits, the routine and the rule for changes, then save it as v1.0.\"],\"wrong\":\"Start from what limits you: the money you can afford to lose. The setup comes before the risk numbers, because the stop depends on it.\",\"explain\":\"Constraints first, then what you trade, then the setup, then the numbers that protect you. The stop and the size depend on the setup, so the risk rules follow it.\",\"note\":{\"key\":\"1.6.2:6\",\"label\":\"Your one setup, in one line (optional)\",\"placeholder\":\"Pullback in an uptrend: higher swing lows, pullback holds above the last one, target at least 2R.\"},\"concept\":\"trading-plan\"},{\"kind\":\"fields\",\"title\":\"Your plan v1 numbers\",\"prompt\":\"Set the numbers of your plan v1. Risk per trade is capped at 2%; 1% is the usual start. The daily limit ends the session after a set loss in R. Save them: they are what you'll check every trade against.\",\"fields\":[{\"id\":\"riskPct\",\"label\":\"Risk per trade, costs included\",\"kind\":\"choice\",\"options\":[0.5,1,2,3],\"unit\":\"%\",\"default\":1},{\"id\":\"dailyLimit\",\"label\":\"Stop for the day after a loss of __R\",\"kind\":\"stepper\",\"min\":1,\"max\":6,\"step\":1,\"unit\":\"R\",\"default\":3},{\"id\":\"maxTrades\",\"label\":\"At most __ trades a day\",\"kind\":\"stepper\",\"min\":1,\"max\":10,\"step\":1,\"default\":3}],\"valid\":{\"field\":\"riskPct\",\"lte\":2},\"correct\":\"Saved as plan v1.0. From now on, judge every trade against these numbers, and change them only through your rule for changes.\",\"feedback\":[{\"when\":{\"field\":\"riskPct\",\"gt\":2},\"text\":\"At 3% per trade, ten losses in a row would cost 26.3% of the account. Plan v1 caps risk at 2% per trade.\"}],\"concept\":\"trading-plan\"}],\"check\":[\"q-1.6.2-1\",\"q-1.6.2-2\",\"q-1.6.2-3\"],\"recap\":{\"takeaways\":[\"Plan v1 is short and checkable: one market, one setup, risk rules, exits and limits.\",\"Risk capital is money you can lose entirely; your limits are numbers a ticket can check.\",\"Change rules only through the plan's own rule: after 30 trades, between sessions, reason written.\"]}},\"1.6.3\":{\"unit\":\"1.6\",\"courseId\":\"1.6.3\",\"hook\":{\"prompt\":\"Pilots and surgeons run checklists for routine steps. Which trading mistake is a checklist most likely to catch?\",\"control\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"pattern\",\"label\":\"A misread chart pattern\",\"feedback\":\"A checklist can ask whether the setup is in your playbook, but it can't read the chart for you.\"},{\"id\":\"nostop\",\"label\":\"Entering with no stop\",\"feedback\":\"Right. A skipped routine step is exactly what checklists catch.\"},{\"id\":\"market\",\"label\":\"A bad market\",\"feedback\":\"No list can change the market. It can only make sure your own steps are done.\"}],\"answer\":\"nostop\"},\"compare\":\"You chose “{yours}”. A checklist catches skipped routine steps, like entering with no stop. It can't read a chart or fix a market.\",\"concept\":\"pre-trade-checklist\"},\"learn\":[{\"kind\":\"explain\",\"text\":\"A [[pre-trade-checklist|pre-trade checklist]] is 5 to 9 yes-or-no questions you answer at the moment of decision, just before the order goes in. It doesn't find trades. It stops you skipping steps you already know, when excitement or boredom would. The evidence comes from aviation and surgery, not from trading, but the failure it targets is the same.\"},{\"kind\":\"figure\",\"title\":\"Your checklist\",\"text\":\"Seven questions, in the order you meet them. A trade needs a yes to every one.\",\"figure\":{\"kind\":\"flow\",\"start\":\"c1\",\"nodes\":[{\"id\":\"c1\",\"text\":\"Setup in my playbook?\",\"kind\":\"question\",\"yes\":\"c2\",\"no\":\"nogo\"},{\"id\":\"c2\",\"text\":\"Every condition yes?\",\"kind\":\"question\",\"yes\":\"c3\",\"no\":\"nogo\"},{\"id\":\"c3\",\"text\":\"Stop at the invalidation?\",\"kind\":\"question\",\"yes\":\"c4\",\"no\":\"nogo\"},{\"id\":\"c4\",\"text\":\"Size within 1%, costs included?\",\"kind\":\"question\",\"yes\":\"c5\",\"no\":\"resize\"},{\"id\":\"c5\",\"text\":\"Daily limit OK?\",\"kind\":\"question\",\"yes\":\"c6\",\"no\":\"nogo\"},{\"id\":\"c6\",\"text\":\"No pause running?\",\"kind\":\"question\",\"yes\":\"c7\",\"no\":\"nogo\"},{\"id\":\"c7\",\"text\":\"Calm enough: 3 of 5 or lower?\",\"kind\":\"question\",\"yes\":\"go\",\"no\":\"nogo\"},{\"id\":\"go\",\"text\":\"Go: send the order\",\"kind\":\"end\"},{\"id\":\"resize\",\"text\":\"Resize within the limit, or skip\",\"kind\":\"end\"},{\"id\":\"nogo\",\"text\":\"No trade\",\"kind\":\"end\"}],\"steps\":[\"Setup first: is it in your playbook, and is every condition a yes?\",\"Then risk: a stop at the invalidation, and a size within 1% with costs.\",\"Then limits and you: daily limit, no pause, and calm at 3 of 5 or lower.\",\"Seven yeses: go. A 'no' on size: resize or skip. Any other 'no': no trade.\"]},\"concept\":\"pre-trade-checklist\"},{\"kind\":\"match\",\"title\":\"Who can check it?\",\"prompt\":\"Some questions can be verified from the ticket and your account. Others only you can answer. Sort each one.\",\"pairs\":[{\"left\":\"A stop on the order?\",\"right\":\"The app can verify\",\"wrong\":\"The stop is a field on the ticket: it's either there or not. That's a check the app can make.\"},{\"left\":\"Size within 1%, costs included?\",\"right\":\"The app can verify\",\"wrong\":\"Size, stop and equity are all on the ticket, so the loss at the stop can be computed for you.\"},{\"left\":\"Daily limit OK?\",\"right\":\"The app can verify\",\"wrong\":\"Today's results are in your account history, so the limit can be checked automatically.\"},{\"left\":\"No pause running?\",\"right\":\"The app can verify\",\"wrong\":\"A pause is a timer the app can see. It doesn't need your judgement.\"},{\"left\":\"Setup in my playbook?\",\"right\":\"Only you can answer\",\"wrong\":\"The app can test single conditions, like a close above a level. Whether the chart shows your setup is your call.\"},{\"left\":\"Every condition yes?\",\"right\":\"Only you can answer\",\"wrong\":\"The app can help with some conditions, but reading the chart against your playbook stays your job.\"},{\"left\":\"Calm enough: 3 of 5 or lower?\",\"right\":\"Only you can answer\",\"wrong\":\"No ticket shows how you feel. Only you can rate it, honestly.\"}],\"correct\":\"The app can catch the number errors. The setup, the conditions and your state stay your job.\",\"concept\":\"pre-trade-checklist\"},{\"kind\":\"predict\",\"title\":\"One 'no'\",\"prompt\":\"Six yeses and one 'no': buying 65 units at 50.00 with the stop at 48.00, the loss at the stop is 133.19 with costs, 1.3% of 10,000.00. Your plan allows 1%. What now?\",\"control\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"anyway\",\"label\":\"Trade anyway\",\"feedback\":\"One 'no' is still a 'no'. A little over today becomes a habit of being over.\"},{\"id\":\"resize\",\"label\":\"Resize within the limit, or skip\",\"feedback\":\"Right. Size is the one 'no' you can fix on the spot.\"},{\"id\":\"move\",\"label\":\"Move the stop closer, so 65 units fit\",\"feedback\":\"That drags the stop off the invalidation and into the noise. The stop comes from the chart; the size adjusts to it.\"}],\"answer\":\"resize\"},\"reveal\":\"Cut the units until the loss at the stop fits: at 48 units it's 98.36 with costs; 49 would lose 100.41. Size is the only 'no' you can fix this way. Any other 'no' means no trade.\",\"concept\":\"pre-trade-checklist\"},{\"kind\":\"explain\",\"title\":\"Keep it short\",\"text\":\"A checklist only works if you read it. Thirty items get skimmed; seven get read. Its main risk is ticking boxes on autopilot, so tie each answer to a fact you can see: the stop price, the risk in %, how much of today's limit is left.\"},{\"kind\":\"figure\",\"title\":\"Run the checklist\",\"text\":\"Ticket 2: your pullback setup, every condition yes, 48 units at 50.00. The stop field is empty: you plan to watch the trade and exit by hand. Choose a branch at each question.\",\"figure\":{\"kind\":\"flow\",\"start\":\"c1\",\"interactive\":true,\"nodes\":[{\"id\":\"c1\",\"text\":\"Setup in my playbook?\",\"kind\":\"question\",\"yes\":\"c2\",\"no\":\"nogo\",\"correct\":\"yes\",\"explain\":\"It's your pullback setup, from the playbook.\"},{\"id\":\"c2\",\"text\":\"Every condition yes?\",\"kind\":\"question\",\"yes\":\"c3\",\"no\":\"nogo\",\"correct\":\"yes\",\"explain\":\"The ticket says every condition is a yes.\"},{\"id\":\"c3\",\"text\":\"Stop at the invalidation?\",\"kind\":\"question\",\"yes\":\"c4\",\"no\":\"nogo\",\"correct\":\"no\",\"explain\":\"The stop field is empty. Watching the trade and exiting by hand is not a stop.\"},{\"id\":\"c4\",\"text\":\"Size within 1%, costs included?\",\"kind\":\"question\",\"yes\":\"c5\",\"no\":\"resize\"},{\"id\":\"c5\",\"text\":\"Daily limit OK?\",\"kind\":\"question\",\"yes\":\"c6\",\"no\":\"nogo\"},{\"id\":\"c6\",\"text\":\"No pause running?\",\"kind\":\"question\",\"yes\":\"c7\",\"no\":\"nogo\"},{\"id\":\"c7\",\"text\":\"Calm enough: 3 of 5 or lower?\",\"kind\":\"question\",\"yes\":\"go\",\"no\":\"nogo\"},{\"id\":\"go\",\"text\":\"Go: send the order\",\"kind\":\"end\"},{\"id\":\"resize\",\"text\":\"Resize within the limit, or skip\",\"kind\":\"end\"},{\"id\":\"nogo\",\"text\":\"No trade\",\"kind\":\"end\"}],\"steps\":[\"Setup and conditions: yes and yes.\",\"Stop at the invalidation: no. No stop means no trade, at any size.\",\"Fix the ticket first: set the stop at 48.00, under the pullback low, then run the list again.\"]},\"concept\":\"pre-trade-checklist\"},{\"kind\":\"match\",\"title\":\"Four tickets, and one more\",\"prompt\":\"Your plan risks 1% of 10,000.00. Run each ticket through the checklist and decide.\",\"pairs\":[{\"left\":\"Pullback setup, every condition yes, stop at 48.00 under the pullback low, 48 units at 50.00: 98.36 at risk with costs. Limit OK, calm at 2 of 5.\",\"right\":\"Go\",\"wrong\":\"Run the seven questions: every answer is yes, and 98.36 is within 1%. That's a go.\"},{\"left\":\"Every condition yes and the size is fine, but there's no stop on the order.\",\"right\":\"No-go\",\"wrong\":\"A missing stop is a 'no' you can't resize away. Add the stop first, or don't trade.\"},{\"left\":\"Everything yes except size: 65 units at 50.00, stop 48.00, put 1.3% at risk with costs.\",\"right\":\"Resize or skip\",\"wrong\":\"Size is the one 'no' you can fix: at 48 units the loss at the stop fits within 1%.\"},{\"left\":\"A breakout you like, but breakouts aren't in your playbook.\",\"right\":\"No-go\",\"wrong\":\"The first question fails: the setup isn't in your playbook. No size makes it one.\"},{\"left\":\"All yes on the ticket, but after a fast loss you rate yourself 4 of 5.\",\"right\":\"No-go\",\"wrong\":\"Calm enough means 3 of 5 or lower. At 4, the last question is a 'no': no trade for now.\"}],\"correct\":\"Seven yeses: go. A 'no' on size: resize or skip. Any other 'no': no trade.\",\"concept\":\"pre-trade-checklist\"},{\"kind\":\"callout\",\"tone\":\"key\",\"text\":\"The checklist ends the same way whether you trade or not: with a line in your [[journal]].\"}],\"check\":[\"q-1.6.3-1\",\"q-1.6.3-2\",\"q-1.6.3-3\"],\"recap\":{\"takeaways\":[\"Answer 5 to 9 yes-or-no questions at the moment of decision, before every order.\",\"The app can verify stop, size and limits; the setup, conditions and your state are yours.\",\"Any 'no' means no trade. A 'no' on size alone: resize within the limit, or skip.\"]}},\"1.6.4\":{\"unit\":\"1.6\",\"courseId\":\"1.6.4\",\"hook\":{\"prompt\":\"Which journal entry is most useful a month later?\",\"control\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"a\",\"label\":\"Lost 98.36. Bad luck\",\"feedback\":\"The number is there, but not the decision. A month later you can't tell whether it was a good trade that lost.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"label\":\"Pullback setup, all three conditions yes. Stop 48.00 under support, 48 units, −1R at the stop. Calm, 2 of 5. Plan followed\",\"feedback\":\"Right. It records the setup, the risk, your state and the plan check, so the decision can be judged.\"},{\"id\":\"c\",\"label\":\"Market was crazy today\",\"feedback\":\"A mood about the market, nothing about your decision. It can't be reviewed or counted.\"}],\"answer\":\"b\"},\"compare\":\"You picked “{yours}”. The useful entry records the setup, the conditions, the risk, your state and the plan check. A month later, it lets you judge the decision, not just the result.\",\"concept\":\"journaling\"},\"learn\":[{\"kind\":\"explain\",\"title\":\"Two halves\",\"text\":\"A [[journal]] entry has two halves. The simulator fills in the numbers: time, setup, entry, stop, target, size, planned [[r|R]], result in R and costs. You add what only you know: your thesis, the [[invalidation]] price, whether you followed the plan, your emotion from 1 to 5, and one lesson. That takes about 30 seconds.\"},{\"kind\":\"figure\",\"title\":\"What the simulator logs\",\"text\":\"One closed LABX trade, as the simulator records it.\",\"figure\":{\"kind\":\"chart\",\"chart\":{\"candles\":[{\"o\":47.2,\"h\":47.6,\"l\":47,\"c\":47.5},{\"o\":47.5,\"h\":48.1,\"l\":47.4,\"c\":47.95},{\"o\":47.95,\"h\":48.6,\"l\":47.8,\"c\":48.45},{\"o\":48.45,\"h\":49.2,\"l\":48.3,\"c\":49.05},{\"o\":49.05,\"h\":49.7,\"l\":48.9,\"c\":49.55},{\"o\":49.55,\"h\":49.65,\"l\":48.9,\"c\":49},{\"o\":49,\"h\":49.1,\"l\":48.2,\"c\":48.4},{\"o\":48.4,\"h\":49,\"l\":48.3,\"c\":48.9},{\"o\":48.9,\"h\":49.6,\"l\":48.8,\"c\":49.45},{\"o\":49.45,\"h\":50.1,\"l\":49.35,\"c\":50},{\"o\":50,\"h\":50.7,\"l\":49.9,\"c\":50.55},{\"o\":50.55,\"h\":50.9,\"l\":50.2,\"c\":50.3},{\"o\":50.3,\"h\":50.4,\"l\":49.2,\"c\":49.4},{\"o\":49.4,\"h\":49.5,\"l\":48.1,\"c\":48.35},{\"o\":48.35,\"h\":49.1,\"l\":48.25,\"c\":48.9},{\"o\":48.9,\"h\":49.3,\"l\":48.4,\"c\":48.55},{\"o\":48.55,\"h\":48.7,\"l\":47.6,\"c\":47.8},{\"o\":47.8,\"h\":47.9,\"l\":46.8,\"c\":47.1}]},\"steps\":[{\"text\":\"Entry 50.00, 48 units, stop 48.00, target 54.00. Planned risk: 98.36 with costs, 1R.\",\"layers\":[{\"kind\":\"level\",\"price\":50,\"role\":\"entry\",\"label\":\"Entry 50.00\"},{\"kind\":\"level\",\"price\":48,\"role\":\"stop\",\"label\":\"Planned stop 48.00\"},{\"kind\":\"level\",\"price\":54,\"role\":\"target\",\"label\":\"Target 54.00\"}]},{\"text\":\"It logs every stop change: 48.00 to 47.00 here, as price dipped to 48.10.\",\"layers\":[{\"kind\":\"path\",\"points\":[{\"index\":9,\"price\":48},{\"index\":13,\"price\":48},{\"index\":13,\"price\":47},{\"index\":17,\"price\":47}],\"role\":\"down\",\"label\":\"Stop\"}]},{\"text\":\"Exit at 47.00: −146.33 with costs, or −1.49R.\",\"layers\":[{\"kind\":\"marker\",\"index\":17,\"price\":47,\"label\":\"Exit 47.00\",\"role\":\"down\"}]},{\"text\":\"What it can't log: your thesis, invalidation, plan check, emotion and lesson.\"}]},\"concept\":\"journaling\"},{\"kind\":\"match\",\"title\":\"What each field is for\",\"prompt\":\"Each written field answers a question a review will ask. Match them.\",\"columns\":[\"Field\",\"What it's for\"],\"pairs\":[{\"left\":\"Thesis\",\"right\":\"What you expected and why\",\"wrong\":\"The thesis is your reason for the trade, written as it was at entry.\"},{\"left\":\"Invalidation\",\"right\":\"Where you'd be proven wrong\",\"wrong\":\"Invalidation is a price: the level where your idea stops being true.\"},{\"left\":\"Emotion, 1 to 5\",\"right\":\"Patterns in how you feel\",\"wrong\":\"One rating means little. Across 30 trades it shows whether you trade worse when you're tense.\"},{\"left\":\"Rule followed?\",\"right\":\"Decision Quality and Risk Discipline\",\"wrong\":\"This yes or no is what the decision scores are built on.\"},{\"left\":\"Lesson\",\"right\":\"What changes next time\",\"wrong\":\"The lesson looks forward: one thing to keep or change.\"}],\"correct\":\"Five short fields, each one feeding a review.\",\"concept\":\"journaling\"},{\"kind\":\"predict\",\"title\":\"Only the losers?\",\"prompt\":\"You journal only your losing trades. What does the journal end up showing?\",\"control\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"fair\",\"label\":\"A fair record\",\"feedback\":\"Every winning trade is missing, including the ones that broke rules. That's not a fair sample.\"},{\"id\":\"tilted\",\"label\":\"A record tilted towards what went wrong\",\"feedback\":\"Right. Losses look like the whole story, and rule-breaking wins stay hidden.\"},{\"id\":\"nothing\",\"label\":\"Nothing useful\",\"feedback\":\"Losses still teach something. The problem is the tilt: without the wins, you can't compare.\"}],\"answer\":\"tilted\"},\"reveal\":\"A selective journal is a biased sample. Log every trade, wins included, or you can't tell a setup that works from one that only feels like it does. A profitable trade that broke a rule is exactly the one you need to see.\",\"concept\":\"journaling\"},{\"kind\":\"explain\",\"title\":\"No trade, no delay\",\"text\":\"Log your no-trade decisions too: the setup you saw, the condition that failed, and that you followed the plan. Write within minutes, not days: once you know what price did next, [[hindsight-bias|hindsight]] rewrites what you thought at entry. Your journal is the data behind every review and every process KPI.\"},{\"kind\":\"predict\",\"title\":\"Rule followed?\",\"prompt\":\"Now journal the trade from before. The simulator has filled in the numbers, including the stop change. First field: rule followed?\",\"figure\":{\"kind\":\"chart\",\"chart\":{\"candles\":[{\"o\":47.2,\"h\":47.6,\"l\":47,\"c\":47.5},{\"o\":47.5,\"h\":48.1,\"l\":47.4,\"c\":47.95},{\"o\":47.95,\"h\":48.6,\"l\":47.8,\"c\":48.45},{\"o\":48.45,\"h\":49.2,\"l\":48.3,\"c\":49.05},{\"o\":49.05,\"h\":49.7,\"l\":48.9,\"c\":49.55},{\"o\":49.55,\"h\":49.65,\"l\":48.9,\"c\":49},{\"o\":49,\"h\":49.1,\"l\":48.2,\"c\":48.4},{\"o\":48.4,\"h\":49,\"l\":48.3,\"c\":48.9},{\"o\":48.9,\"h\":49.6,\"l\":48.8,\"c\":49.45},{\"o\":49.45,\"h\":50.1,\"l\":49.35,\"c\":50},{\"o\":50,\"h\":50.7,\"l\":49.9,\"c\":50.55},{\"o\":50.55,\"h\":50.9,\"l\":50.2,\"c\":50.3},{\"o\":50.3,\"h\":50.4,\"l\":49.2,\"c\":49.4},{\"o\":49.4,\"h\":49.5,\"l\":48.1,\"c\":48.35},{\"o\":48.35,\"h\":49.1,\"l\":48.25,\"c\":48.9},{\"o\":48.9,\"h\":49.3,\"l\":48.4,\"c\":48.55},{\"o\":48.55,\"h\":48.7,\"l\":47.6,\"c\":47.8},{\"o\":47.8,\"h\":47.9,\"l\":46.8,\"c\":47.1}],\"layers\":[{\"kind\":\"level\",\"price\":50,\"role\":\"entry\",\"label\":\"Entry 50.00\"},{\"kind\":\"level\",\"price\":48,\"role\":\"stop\",\"label\":\"Planned stop 48.00\"},{\"kind\":\"path\",\"points\":[{\"index\":9,\"price\":48},{\"index\":13,\"price\":48},{\"index\":13,\"price\":47},{\"index\":17,\"price\":47}],\"role\":\"down\",\"label\":\"Stop\"},{\"kind\":\"marker\",\"index\":17,\"price\":47,\"label\":\"Exit 47.00\",\"role\":\"down\"}]},\"steps\":[{\"text\":\"The plan put the stop at 48.00. At 47.00 the loss was −1.49R, not −1R.\"}]},\"control\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"yes\",\"label\":\"Yes: the trade had a stop all along\",\"feedback\":\"The log shows the stop moved from 48.00 to 47.00. That breaks the plan.\"},{\"id\":\"no\",\"label\":\"No: the stop was moved further away\",\"feedback\":\"Right. Moving the stop from 48.00 to 47.00 raised the loss at the stop from 98.36 to 146.33.\"},{\"id\":\"cant\",\"label\":\"Can't tell without the next candles\",\"feedback\":\"What price did next doesn't change the answer. The rule was about the stop, and the log shows it moved.\"}],\"answer\":\"no\"},\"reveal\":\"Answer 'Rule followed?' from the log, never from the result. The same stop move would break the plan even if the trade had ended in profit.\",\"concept\":\"journaling\"},{\"kind\":\"fields\",\"title\":\"Your part of the entry\",\"prompt\":\"Fill in two fields. Invalidation: the price where the idea was proven wrong, as set at entry, not where the stop ended up. Emotion: how you would have felt during this trade, from 1 (calm) to 5 (very tense).\",\"fields\":[{\"id\":\"invalidation\",\"label\":\"Invalidation price\",\"kind\":\"choice\",\"options\":[47,48,50,54],\"default\":50},{\"id\":\"emotion\",\"label\":\"Emotion during the trade: __ of 5\",\"kind\":\"stepper\",\"min\":1,\"max\":5,\"step\":1,\"default\":3}],\"valid\":{\"field\":\"invalidation\",\"eq\":48},\"correct\":\"Saved. Invalidation at 48.00, under the pullback low, as planned at entry. The emotion rating is yours: across 30 trades it shows patterns.\",\"feedback\":[{\"when\":{\"field\":\"invalidation\",\"eq\":47},\"text\":\"47.00 is where the stop ended up, not where the idea was wrong. At entry, the plan put the invalidation at 48.00, under the pullback low.\"},{\"when\":{\"field\":\"invalidation\",\"eq\":50},\"text\":\"50.00 is the entry. The invalidation is the price that proves the idea wrong: 48.00, under the pullback low.\"},{\"when\":{\"field\":\"invalidation\",\"eq\":54},\"text\":\"54.00 is the target, where the idea pays. The invalidation is where it fails: 48.00.\"}],\"concept\":\"journaling\"},{\"kind\":\"order\",\"title\":\"Your 30 seconds\",\"prompt\":\"Put the written part in order, then add your lesson from this trade.\",\"items\":[\"Check the numbers the simulator filled in.\",\"Write the thesis and invalidation as they were at entry.\",\"Mark 'Rule followed?' from the log, and rate your emotion.\",\"Write one lesson for next time.\"],\"wrong\":\"Facts first, then what you knew at entry, then the check, and the lesson last.\",\"explain\":\"Facts first, then what you knew at entry, then the check, and the lesson last, once everything else is on the page.\",\"note\":{\"key\":\"1.6.4:7\",\"label\":\"Your lesson from this trade (optional)\",\"placeholder\":\"Keep the stop where the plan put it, even when price comes close.\"},\"concept\":\"journaling\"}],\"check\":[\"q-1.6.4-1\",\"q-1.6.4-2\",\"q-1.6.4-3\"],\"recap\":{\"takeaways\":[\"Log every trade and no-trade: thesis, invalidation, plan check, emotion and one lesson.\",\"The simulator fills in the numbers; your 30 seconds add what only you know.\",\"Journaling only losers, or days later, tilts the record and lets hindsight rewrite it.\"]}},\"1.6.6\":{\"unit\":\"1.6\",\"courseId\":\"1.6.6\",\"hook\":{\"prompt\":\"Five losses in a row, each following every rule at 1% risk. What should change?\",\"control\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"setup\",\"label\":\"The setup: it stopped working\",\"feedback\":\"Five trades can't show that. Methods that make money still lose five in a row, and often.\"},{\"id\":\"nothing\",\"label\":\"Nothing yet: that's within normal variance\",\"feedback\":\"Right. Every rule was followed, so these losses are the normal cost of trading.\"},{\"id\":\"double\",\"label\":\"Double the size to win it back\",\"feedback\":\"That's the revenge pattern. It turns a normal streak into a deep drawdown.\"}],\"answer\":\"nothing\"},\"compare\":\"You chose “{yours}”. With every rule followed, nothing should change yet. At a 40% win rate, a run of five or more losses shows up in 97.6% of 100-trade sequences.\",\"concept\":\"mistake-vs-variance\"},\"learn\":[{\"kind\":\"explain\",\"title\":\"Two buckets\",\"text\":\"Every losing trade goes into one of two buckets. [[variance|Variance]] is a valid trade that lost: the plan was followed, and the loss is the normal cost of trading. A **mistake** is a break in the process: a missing stop, an oversized position, a broken rule. Variance can't be fixed. Mistakes can.\"},{\"kind\":\"match\",\"title\":\"Which bucket?\",\"prompt\":\"Six losing trades from one month. Sort each into Variance or Mistake.\",\"pairs\":[{\"left\":\"All rules followed, stopped at −1R\",\"right\":\"Variance\",\"wrong\":\"Every rule was followed. A loss on its own isn't a mistake.\"},{\"left\":\"Entered without a stop\",\"right\":\"Mistake\",\"wrong\":\"Losing isn't the issue: entering without a stop broke the process.\"},{\"left\":\"Stop moved away, lost −2R\",\"right\":\"Mistake\",\"wrong\":\"The plan allowed −1R. Moving the stop doubled the loss: that's the process, not the market.\"},{\"left\":\"Gap through the stop, −1.4R, sized at 1%\",\"right\":\"Variance\",\"wrong\":\"Size and stop were right. A gap past the stop is a market event, not a broken rule.\"},{\"left\":\"Tripled the size after a loss\",\"right\":\"Mistake\",\"wrong\":\"Sizing up to win it back breaks the risk rule, whatever the result.\"},{\"left\":\"Valid setup, target missed by 0.05, then stopped\",\"right\":\"Variance\",\"wrong\":\"So close hurts, but the plan was followed. Near misses are variance.\"}],\"correct\":\"Three of each. Note the gap: −1.4R and still variance, because the size and the stop were right.\",\"concept\":\"mistake-vs-variance\"},{\"kind\":\"explain\",\"title\":\"Name the mistake\",\"text\":\"Each mistake gets an [[error-tag|error tag]], the app's fixed name for it, so you can count them: Entering without a stop, Risking more than planned, Position too large, Stop inside normal noise, Chasing extended moves, Moving the stop further away, Sizing up after a loss, Trading too often, Breaking your playbook, Misreading your own conditions.\"},{\"kind\":\"worked\",\"title\":\"Error cost\",\"lines\":[\"Moving the stop further away: lost −2R where the plan allowed −1R. Error cost: −1R.\",\"Sizing up after a loss: lost −3R where the plan allowed −1R. Error cost: −2R.\",\"Chasing extended moves, outside the plan: lost −1R where the plan said no trade, 0R. Error cost: −1R.\",\"Total error cost = ?\"],\"ask\":{\"answer\":-4,\"tolerance\":0,\"unit\":\"R\",\"feedback\":[{\"value\":4,\"text\":\"Right size, but it's a cost: write it as −4.\"},{\"value\":-6,\"text\":\"That's everything these trades lost. Take away what the plan allowed: −6R − (−2R).\"}],\"correct\":\"Right: −4R. That much came from the process, not the market.\"},\"after\":\"Variance has no error cost: it was the plan working. Count your error cost each week, and you'll know which rule to protect first.\",\"concept\":\"error-taxonomy\"},{\"kind\":\"predict\",\"title\":\"How unusual?\",\"prompt\":\"Your method wins 40% of its trades. You've just lost six in a row, every rule followed. Over 100 trades, how unusual is a run like that?\",\"control\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"rare\",\"label\":\"Very rare: something must be broken\",\"feedback\":\"It feels rare, but 100 trades hold many stretches of six. One of them going all wrong is likely.\"},{\"id\":\"common\",\"label\":\"Common: it shows up in almost 9 of 10 sets of 100 trades\",\"feedback\":\"Right: 87.3%, assuming each trade's result is independent of the last.\"}],\"answer\":\"common\"},\"reveal\":\"At a 40% win rate, a run of six or more losses shows up in 87.3% of 100-trade sequences. A streak on its own is not evidence of a mistake. The journal is: look for error tags, not at the length of the run.\",\"concept\":\"mistake-vs-variance\"},{\"kind\":\"callout\",\"tone\":\"key\",\"text\":\"Change rules for mistakes, not for variance. Every rule change still goes through your plan's own rule for changes.\"},{\"kind\":\"match\",\"title\":\"Tag your journal\",\"prompt\":\"Eight losses from your journal. Put each one in Variance, or tag the mistake with its error name.\",\"pairs\":[{\"left\":\"Every condition met, stop kept, stopped out at −1R\",\"right\":\"Variance\",\"wrong\":\"Nothing was broken: valid setup, stop kept, −1R. That's variance.\"},{\"left\":\"No stop on the order; closed by hand at −1.8R\",\"right\":\"Entering without a stop\",\"wrong\":\"There was no stop when the order went in. That has its own tag.\"},{\"left\":\"Stop moved from 48.00 to 47.00 as price came close; −1.5R\",\"right\":\"Moving the stop further away\",\"wrong\":\"The stop moved away from price, raising the risk. Find the tag that names exactly that.\"},{\"left\":\"Doubled the size after two losses, to win it back; −2R\",\"right\":\"Sizing up after a loss\",\"wrong\":\"A bigger size right after losses, to recover: that's sizing up after a loss.\"},{\"left\":\"Breakout trade, but breakouts aren't in the playbook; −1R\",\"right\":\"Breaking your playbook\",\"wrong\":\"The setup isn't in your playbook, so the plan's answer was no trade.\"},{\"left\":\"Price gapped through the stop; −1.3R, sized at 1%\",\"right\":\"Variance\",\"wrong\":\"The size and the stop were right. The gap is a market event, so it's variance.\"},{\"left\":\"Entered on two of three conditions; −1R\",\"right\":\"Breaking your playbook\",\"wrong\":\"Every condition must be yes. Two of three means the playbook said no trade.\"},{\"left\":\"Fourth loss in a row, all rules followed; −1R\",\"right\":\"Variance\",\"wrong\":\"A streak isn't a mistake. Every rule was followed, so it's variance.\"}],\"correct\":\"Three variance, five mistakes, four tags. The tags show which rule to protect; the variance asks for no change at all.\",\"concept\":\"error-taxonomy\"}],\"check\":[\"q-1.6.6-1\",\"q-1.6.6-2\",\"q-1.6.6-3\"],\"recap\":{\"takeaways\":[\"Variance is a valid trade that lost; a mistake is a broken process. Only mistakes get fixed.\",\"Tag each mistake with its error name, and count what mistakes cost in R.\",\"A losing streak with every rule followed is variance: six in a row is common at 40%.\"]}},\"1.6.7\":{\"unit\":\"1.6\",\"courseId\":\"1.6.7\",\"hook\":{\"prompt\":\"After 30 trades, Trader A is up 6% with 8 trades taken without a stop. Trader B is down 2% with every trade by the plan. Who is closer to passing Level 1?\",\"control\":{\"kind\":\"choice\",\"choices\":[{\"id\":\"a\",\"label\":\"Trader A\",\"feedback\":\"A's profit doesn't count toward the level. 22 of 30 trades with a stop is 73.3%, far below the 95% needed.\"},{\"id\":\"b\",\"label\":\"Trader B\",\"feedback\":\"Right. Level 1 measures process: B's stops and sizes meet the bar, and profit doesn't count.\"},{\"id\":\"neither\",\"label\":\"Neither\",\"feedback\":\"Both still need plan v1 and Capstone 1, but only B's 30 trades meet the process bar. Profit doesn't count.\"}],\"answer\":\"b\"},\"compare\":\"You picked “{yours}”. Trader B is closer: Level 1 counts stops, sizes and limits, not profit. Trader A's stops: 22 ÷ 30 = 73.3%, below the 95% needed.\",\"concept\":\"process-kpis\"},\"learn\":[{\"kind\":\"explain\",\"title\":\"Measure the process\",\"text\":\"[[process-kpi|Process KPIs]] measure how well you follow your plan, not what the market paid. Five matter at Level 1: [[plan-adherence|plan adherence]], [[risk-accuracy|risk accuracy]], [[stop-integrity|stop integrity]], limit compliance and journal completeness. Each is the share of trades, or days, that followed a rule, so every one of them is in your hands.\"},{\"kind\":\"worked\",\"title\":\"Stop integrity\",\"lines\":[\"30 trades in your journal.\",\"29 had a stop at entry, and none was moved further away.\",\"Stop integrity = 29 ÷ 30 = ?\"],\"ask\":{\"answer\":96.7,\"tolerance\":0.1,\"unit\":\"%\",\"feedback\":[{\"value\":0.97,\"text\":\"That's the fraction. As a percentage, multiply by 100.\"},{\"value\":3.3,\"text\":\"That's the share that failed. Stop integrity counts the trades that passed: 29 of 30.\"}],\"correct\":\"Right: 96.7%. Above the 95% the Level 1 gate asks for.\"},\"concept\":\"process-kpis\"},{\"kind\":\"figure\",\"title\":\"Why not profit?\",\"text\":\"A good system still ends short stretches in the red, and the shorter the stretch, the more often. Over 20 trades it's about 1 time in 8, so profit says little at that size. Process KPIs don't depend on luck: 20 or 30 trades already tell you something real.\",\"figure\":{\"kind\":\"bars\",\"unit\":\"%\",\"bars\":[{\"label\":\"5 trades\",\"value\":33.7,\"role\":\"down\"},{\"label\":\"10 trades\",\"value\":16.7,\"role\":\"down\"},{\"label\":\"20 trades\",\"value\":12.6,\"role\":\"down\"},{\"label\":\"50 trades\",\"value\":5.4,\"role\":\"down\"},{\"label\":\"100 trades\",\"value\":0.8,\"role\":\"down\"}],\"steps\":[\"Chance of a net loss for a system that wins 40% at +2.5R and loses 60% at −1R.\",\"That's +0.4R a trade, yet 12.6% of 20-trade stretches still end in a loss.\"]},\"concept\":\"process-kpis\"},{\"kind\":\"match\",\"title\":\"KPI and formula\",\"prompt\":\"Each KPI is a simple share. Match it to its formula.\",\"columns\":[\"KPI\",\"Formula\"],\"pairs\":[{\"left\":\"Stop integrity\",\"right\":\"Trades with a stop at entry, never widened ÷ all trades\",\"wrong\":\"Stop integrity is about the stop: there at entry, and never moved further away.\"},{\"left\":\"Risk accuracy\",\"right\":\"Trades sized within the rule ÷ all trades\",\"wrong\":\"Risk accuracy checks the size: the loss at the stop, with costs, within your rule.\"},{\"left\":\"Plan adherence\",\"right\":\"Trades that match a playbook setup ÷ all trades\",\"wrong\":\"Plan adherence asks whether the trade was a playbook setup at all.\"},{\"left\":\"Limit compliance\",\"right\":\"Days within your limits ÷ days traded\",\"wrong\":\"Limits are set per day, so this one counts days, not trades.\"}],\"correct\":\"Every one is a count you can check from the journal, with no luck involved.\",\"concept\":\"process-kpis\"},{\"kind\":\"explain\",\"title\":\"Process goals\",\"text\":\"Set goals you control. 'A stop at entry on 100% of trades this week' is a process goal: you can meet it every time. 'Make 5% this month' is an outcome goal: luck decides much of it, and chasing it pushes you towards positions that are too large.\"},{\"kind\":\"callout\",\"tone\":\"key\",\"text\":\"The Level 1 gate: 30 simulated trades, with a stop before entry in at least 95% and correct risk in at least 90%, no limit broken, plan v1 written, and Capstone 1 passed.\"},{\"kind\":\"match\",\"title\":\"Your 20-trade log\",\"prompt\":\"Your log: 20 trades. Trade 4's stop was moved further away. Trades 9 and 12 risked 1.4% and 1.6% with costs; your rule is 1%. Trades 9, 15 and 18 weren't playbook setups. Every day stayed within your limits. Match each KPI to its value.\",\"columns\":[\"KPI\",\"Value\"],\"pairs\":[{\"left\":\"Stop integrity\",\"right\":\"95.0%\",\"wrong\":\"Only trade 4 broke stop integrity: 19 ÷ 20.\"},{\"left\":\"Risk accuracy\",\"right\":\"90.0%\",\"wrong\":\"Trades 9 and 12 were oversized, so 18 of 20 were sized within the rule.\"},{\"left\":\"Plan adherence\",\"right\":\"85.0%\",\"wrong\":\"Three trades weren't playbook setups: 17 ÷ 20.\"},{\"left\":\"Limit compliance\",\"right\":\"100%\",\"wrong\":\"It counts days, and every day stayed within the limits.\"}],\"correct\":\"95.0%, 90.0% and 85.0%: stops and risk meet the gate; adherence has room to grow. Trade 9 counted against two KPIs.\",\"concept\":\"process-kpis\"},{\"kind\":\"order\",\"title\":\"Your next 30 trades\",\"prompt\":\"Put your next block of 30 trades in order. Then write one process goal for it.\",\"items\":[\"Save plan v1 and start the count.\",\"Run the checklist before every order.\",\"Journal every trade and no-trade within minutes.\",\"After 30 trades, work out your KPIs.\",\"Pick the weakest KPI as your next process goal.\"],\"wrong\":\"Start from the plan: nothing counts before it's saved. The KPIs come from the journal, and the goal comes from the KPIs.\",\"explain\":\"Plan, checklist, journal, KPIs, goal: the loop you'll repeat for every block of 30 trades.\",\"note\":{\"key\":\"1.6.7:7\",\"label\":\"Your process goal for the next 30 trades (optional)\",\"placeholder\":\"A stop at entry on 100% of trades.\"},\"concept\":\"process-kpis\"}],\"check\":[\"q-1.6.7-1\",\"q-1.6.7-2\",\"q-1.6.7-3\"],\"recap\":{\"takeaways\":[\"Stop integrity, risk accuracy and plan adherence are simple shares of trades that followed a rule.\",\"Over 20 trades, profit is mostly luck; process KPIs already mean something.\",\"Set one process goal you control for your next 30 trades, not a profit target.\"]}}}");
